Garbage
Seeing such a package, I ask everyone: don’t you think it looks like trash that just got thrown on the side of the road?
A plastic, fragile package – which was simply sent from Germany using a regular plastic bag. Is such packaging really appropriate for such products?
I think such packaging is suitable for trash only. The product itself is purchased in a very basic, poorly designed package that provides no protection against damage at all; it’s just a simple plastic bag. Upon receipt, the package is completely deformed, and the items inside are also damaged.
If I had just encountered one of these products, I would have accepted it. I bought several products, and all of them were in the same condition. I contacted Amazon customer service, who said that I could return the products, but the shipping cost would have to be prepaid. The shipping cost was then refunded to me in the form of a gift card.
I’d like to ask: I pay for the shipping costs in cash, and you offer me a gift card as a refund. But if you want me to buy the gift card myself, just say so clearly. Moreover, I have to mail the product to the warehouse in Germany myself. Isn’t that just creating extra trouble for me simply because I want to purchase a product?
And I’ve been telling the customer service all along who is responsible for such problems, but they refuse to admit even a single word that it’s their fault—they don’t even dare to take any responsibility. What kind of after-sales service is this, then? In one word: they should just admit their mistake! But I guess Amazon won’t even give my review a chance to be published; they’ll just delete it directly.
